<LessonLayout title="The Commandments I-III" cic={lessonRef} scripture={lessonScripture}>

<section class="content">

<h2>Big Question</h2>

<p class="big-question">How do we love God above all things?</p>


<p>
In Nazareth, there was a carpenter. His name was Joseph. Day after day, year after year, he worked with wood: measuring, cutting, sanding, building. And a child watched him. The Son of God learned to work from a humble carpenter. Before Jesus preached, before He healed, before He walked on water, He worked. For eighteen years. The God of the universe swept floors and carried lumber. The Church teaches that work is not a curse — it is a participation in God's creative action. The first three commandments call us to love God above all: no other gods, no idols, keep His name holy, keep the Sabbath. Work becomes worship when offered to God. St. Josemaría Escrivá put it simply: "Your daily work is not something secondary — it is an essential part of your path to holiness."
</p>


</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>Understanding the Teaching</h2>

<p>The Catechism of the Catholic Church provides clear guidance on how we are to live as followers of Christ. This teaching is not a burden but a path to true freedom and happiness.</p>

<div class="depth-box depth-box--semilla">
<h4 class="depth-box__title">Activity</h4>
<p>Consider how this moral teaching applies to decisions you face daily.</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>Biblical Foundation</h2>

<p>Sacred Scripture reveals God's plan for human flourishing. The moral law is not arbitrary but reflects the wisdom of the Creator who knows what leads to human happiness.</p>

<div class="depth-box depth-box--brotes">
<h4 class="depth-box__title">Connection</h4>
<p>Read the Scripture passages and reflect on how they illuminate this teaching.</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>For Reflection</h2>

<ol>
<li>How does this teaching challenge your current way of living?</li>
<li>What practical steps can you take to grow in this area?</li>
<li>How does grace assist us in living this moral teaching?</li>
<li>What obstacles do you face in living according to this teaching?</li>
<li>Who can support you in growing in this aspect of Christian life?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>Key Idea</h2>

<div class="callout">
<p><strong>Key Idea:</strong> The first three commandments teach us to love God with all our heart, soul, and mind.</p>
</div>

</section>

